Claims:
[
    "In the pre-training stage, representative RAG (Retrieval-Augmented Generation) models that incorporate retrieval-augmented mechanisms include REALM, RETRO, and FiD-RAG.",
    "These models deeply integrate the retrieval process from external knowledge bases with language model pre-training, enabling the model to learn to use external information early in training to generate more accurate and factually consistent text.",
    "The mainstream RAG approach typically uses a two-stage paradigm of 'freezing the pre-trained language model + fine-tuning the retriever' (e.g., the original RAG model [Lewis et al., 2020]).",
    "REALM (Retrieval-Augmented Language Model Pre-Training) introduces a learnable retrieval module during pre-training that retrieves relevant documents from corpora such as Wikipedia.",
    "REALM uses a masked language modeling (MLM) objective to jointly optimize both the retriever and encoder, enabling the model to dynamically retrieve relevant information based on context.",
    "In REALM, the retriever is trained end-to-end via backpropagation, achieving joint optimization of retrieval and language understanding.",
    "RETRO (REtrieval-Enhanced TRansfOrmer) embeds the retrieval-augmented mechanism within the Transformer architecture, introducing retrieved chunks (text segments) at each layer or specific layers.",
    "During pre-training, RETRO uses a large-scale corpus (e.g., MassiveText) to construct a retrieval database and performs real-time retrieval of the most relevant chunks during training.",
    "RETRO significantly improves performance on knowledge-intensive tasks and can leverage external knowledge without fine-tuning.",
    "FiD-RAG or Pre-trained Fusion-in-Decoder with Retrieval refers to works that combine FiD with pre-training, although the original FiD was a fine-tuning stage method.",
    "Subsequent research has attempted to adopt a fusion mechanism similar to FiD during the pre-training stage.",
    "FiD-RAG encodes multiple retrieved documents separately and concatenates them as input to the decoder, allowing the model to learn cross-document reasoning during pre-training.",
    "These models share the common feature of breaking the traditional boundary of 'pre-train first, then fine-tune with retrieval,' enabling the model to actively retrieve and integrate external knowledge during pre-training.",
    "This approach enhances factual accuracy, reduces hallucination, and improves coverage of long-tail knowledge."
] 

